# Review is required HERE and deliberately nowhere else.
#
# A gate that every pull request has to pass, on a repository with one backend developer, is a gate
# that gets bypassed every single time — and a control bypassed 100% of the time is not a control,
# it just makes the merge history say something untrue. So `dev` requires no approval in general.
#
# These two files are different. They are the published contract WP5 and WP6 build against: the web
# client and the Android client both hardcode the field names, the enum values and the error codes in
# them. A change here is a change to someone else's code, made without them in the room. That is
# exactly the case where a second reader is worth waiting for.
#
# docs/contract-drift.md is intentionally NOT owned: it is the register of places the code and the
# Contract disagree, and it has to stay cheap to append to or nobody will write drift down.

